{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Go_for_the_Eyes","to":"Go for the Eyes"},{"from":"Force_Field","to":"Force Field"},{"from":"Master_Reality","to":"Master Reality"},{"from":"Boot_Sequence","to":"Boot Sequence"},{"from":"Dagger_Spray","to":"Dagger Spray"},{"from":"Lesson_Learned","to":"Lesson Learned"},{"from":"Battle_Trance","to":"Battle Trance"}],"pages":{"1880":{"pageid":1880,"ns":0,"title":"Battle Trance","revisions":[{"revid":56415,"parentid":55640,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Battle Trance\n| Image       = Red-BattleTrance.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Draw (3;4) cards.<br>You cannot draw additional cards this turn.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, No Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|No Draw}}\n{{C|Battle Trance}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 3 (4 if upgraded) cards and gives one {{BD|No Draw}}, which prevents cards from being drawn for the rest of your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Orange Pellets}} can remove the {{BD|No Draw}} you get from this card.\n* Sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, {{P|Ancient Potion}}, {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}} can prevent this card from applying {{BD|No Draw}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Escape Plan gaining Block when card drawn is blocked by No Draw power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** No Draw power now counts as a debuff.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2127":{"pageid":2127,"ns":0,"title":"Boot Sequence","revisions":[{"revid":56908,"parentid":56447,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Boot Sequence\n|Image       = Blue-BootSequence.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Innate}}.<br>Gain (10;13) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Innate, Block, Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Boot Sequence}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 10 (13 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after being played. It is {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The beta art depicts the [[Defect]] inside of {{R|The Boot}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2084":{"pageid":2084,"ns":0,"title":"Chaos","revisions":[{"revid":56933,"parentid":55688,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Chaos\n|Image       = Blue-Chaos.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{KW|Channel}} (1;2) random (Orb;Orbs).\n|GivesToPlayer = Channel, Lightning, Frost, Dark, Plasma\n}}\n{{C|Chaos}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}. <!---It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 (2) {{KW|Orbs|Orb(s)}}, chosen at random. Like all random effects, the choice of Orb type is seeded. In the case of Chaos+, the two Orbs have no bearing on each other, and may be any combination of types.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}, and Chaos is the only card capable of creating all 4 Orb types.\n\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Chaos works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of non-{{KW|Plasma}} Orbs generated by Chaos: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n* Some Orb types have individual synergies:\n** {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n** {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits an additional time for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n** {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n** {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}} triggers all {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb's}} [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] an additional time.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making non-{{KW|Plasma}} Orbs less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2062":{"pageid":2062,"ns":0,"title":"Claw","revisions":[{"revid":50557,"parentid":36214,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Claw\n|Image       = Blue-Claw.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (3;5) damage.<br>Increase the damage of ALL Claw cards by 2 this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Claw}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* It can be placed into your draw pile or hand to reduce the time before it can be played again:\n** {{C|Hologram}}, {{C|All for One}} and {{P|Liquid Memories}} can place it from the discard pile into your hand.\n** {{C|Reboot}}, {{C|Deep Breath}}, and {{C|Headbutt}} can be used to get it from your discard pile into your draw pile.\n** {{C|Secret Weapon}} can be used to place it from your draw pile into your hand.\n\n* When played multiple times, it also scales multiple times, and the consecutive plays already use the scaling from the previous plays. This can be done with {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Double Tap}}, or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}.\n\n* As playing one {{C|Claw}} scales all {{C|Claw|Claws}} in the deck, it synergizes with itself.\n\n* Increasing the chance of drawing {{C|Claw}} can be done through decreasing the deck size, with cards such as {{C|Recycle}}, or through drawing more cards. \n** {{C|Scrape}} can be used to draw {{C|Claw}}, as it costs 0.\n** {{C|Violence}} will put only {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in your hand.\n** {{R|Unceasing Top}} is very effective with {{C|Claw}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n\n* {{C|Claw|Claws}} added to your deck during combat, through for example {{C|Hello World}} or an {{P|Attack Potion}}, start from their base damage regardless of the amount of {{C|Claw|Claws}} played before.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Before release the name of this card was \"Gash\" and was an {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} card.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Claw card gets VFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1948":{"pageid":1948,"ns":0,"title":"Dagger Spray","revisions":[{"revid":55720,"parentid":50477,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dagger Spray\n|Image       = Green-DaggerSpray.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (4;6) damage to ALL enemies twice.\n}}\n{{C|Dagger Spray}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 damage to '''ALL''' enemies twice.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 2 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 48: Creative AI'''\n** Improved Dagger Spray VFX readability and no longer flashes a sprite for 1 frame at the start.\n** Fixed issue where Dagger Spray VFX wasn't spawning in the right spot for some resolutions.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Dagger Spray card buff.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1461":{"pageid":1461,"ns":0,"title":"Darkness","revisions":[{"revid":56339,"parentid":55726,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Darkness\n| Image       = Blue-Darkness.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Dark}}.(;<br>Trigger the passive ability of ALL {{KW|Dark}} orbs.)\n| GivesToPlayer = Channel, Dark\n| InteractsWith = Dark\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Dark}}\n{{C|Darkness}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}}{{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. <!---It {{KW|Channel|Channels}} a {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}}. Then, if it is upgraded, it triggers the {{KW|Passive|Passives}} of all {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} an additional time.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* As Darkness+ triggers [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] after {{KW|Channel|Channeling}} the {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}}, the Orb just Channeled will receive the extra Passive, but if the first Orb is a {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}} which is {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} as a result, it will not.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Darkness+ benefits any {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} you currently have {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} as well, so it works well with all other sources of {{KW|Dark}}: {{C|Doom and Gloom}}, {{C|Chaos}}, {{C|Rainbow}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}, and {{P|Essence of Darkness}}\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} more frequently.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} less effective.\n** However, as this only affects the future growth of Dark Orbs, the downside is minimized later into fights, once your Orbs have had to time to scale up already. As such, {{C|Hyperbeam}} may work to clear small enemies before {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} your Dark Orbs.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Darkness+ card reworked. Now triggers the passive ability of your Dark Orbs.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Darkness now utilizes UPGRADE_DESCRIPTION for plurality (for non-Eng languages).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1940":{"pageid":1940,"ns":0,"title":"Dropkick","revisions":[{"revid":56766,"parentid":55751,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Dropkick\n| Image       = Red-Dropkick.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (5;8) damage.<br>If the enemy has {{BD|Vulnerable}}, gain {{Icon|RE}} and draw 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Energy\n| InteractsWith = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{C|Dropkick}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (8 if upgraded) damage. If the target has {{BD|Vulnerable}}, gain 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' and draw 1 card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* No matter what {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{C|Dropkick}} has, the player will always gain 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' if it is played on a target with {{BD|Vulnerable}}. This can be used to your advantage by reducing the cost below 1, but can lose you {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' as well if the cost is increased:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Setup}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' gain, although this extra energy is often useless.\n* {{C|Madness}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* If {{C|Dropkick}} is selected from an {{P|Attack Potion}} it will have a cost of 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{BD|Confused}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}} will randomize the cost from 0 to 3, which can result in a neutral, gained or lost amount of energy.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Dropkick card now resolves its actions in order of its description.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Fixed rare crash with Dropkick.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Dropkick, Fire Breathing, and Shockwave portraits weren't rendering in card popup view.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1456":{"pageid":1456,"ns":0,"title":"Dualcast","revisions":[{"revid":56337,"parentid":50549,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Dualcast\n| Image       = Blue-Dualcast.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = {{KW|Evoke}} your next Orb twice.\n| GivesToPlayer = Evoke\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Evoke}}\n{{C|Dualcast}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Obtaining Dualcast ==\nThe [[Defect]] starts the game with one copy of Dualcast in their deck.\n\nDualcast cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\nIf you already have Dualcast in your deck, it can be duplicated using {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} or the {{E|Duplicator}} Event.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Fixed issue where evoked Dark Orbs wouldn't switch targets if the first target died when multi-casting.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1967":{"pageid":1967,"ns":0,"title":"Envenom","revisions":[{"revid":56789,"parentid":56788,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Envenom\n| Image       = Green-Envenom.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = Whenever an Attack deals unblocked damage, apply 1 {{BD|Poison}}.\n| PowerGives = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Envenom\n| Image        = Icon Envenom.png\n| Description  = Whenever you deal unblocked damage, apply X {{BD|Poison}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}\n{{C|Envenom}} is a 2 (1) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If {{C|Bane}} is played on an enemy with no {{BD|Poison}}, 1 will be added by the first hit of Bane, causing the second hit to occur.\n* Although the {{BD|Poison}} applied by Envenom happens at the same time as the hit that caused it (i.e. before the next hit of the Attack), all triggers of {{C|Sadistic Nature}} will be applied after the attack finishes.\n\n==== a) Poison Interactions ====\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Attacks with multiple hits will trigger Envenom multiple times; for example, {{C|Riddle with Holes}}, {{C|Dagger Spray}}, and {{C|Skewer}}.\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}. It applies to each instance of {{BD|Poison}} separately. For instance, if you have Envenom and Snecko Skull, and hit an enemy with {{C|Glass Knife}}, that enemy will get 4 {{BD|Poison}}, not 3.\n\n* {{C|Envenom}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The Attack does have to actually deal damage. If the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}'s {{BD|Invincible}} cap is maxed out for the turn, additional Attacks will not apply any {{BD|Poison}} to it.\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}}.\n** However, certain Attacks allow Envenom to deal several [[Debuffs]] in a single card play, clearing {{BD|Artifact}} for your other {{BD|Poison}} sources.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Envenom's Poison is now applied immediately after the damage occurs.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Envenom power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Envenom card gets a wording update for clarity.\n** Updating description for Envenom power to mention unblocked dmg.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2113":{"pageid":2113,"ns":0,"title":"Fission","revisions":[{"revid":55780,"parentid":53384,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Fission\n|Image       = Blue-Fission.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = (Remove;{{KW|Evoke}}) all your Orbs. Gain {{Icon|BE}} and draw 1 card for each Orb (removed;{{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}).<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Energy\n}}\n{{C|Fission}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It removes (if upgraded it {{KW|Evoke|Evokes}} instead) all of your [[Orbs]], gaining 1 {{Icon|BE}} and drawing a card for each Orb removed (Evoked) this way. Removed Orbs do not trigger their Evoke effects, and are simply deleted.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Cracked Core}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} and {{R|Nuclear Battery}} each give Fission 1 additional Orb to remove ({{KW|Evoke}}) directly from the start of combat. {{C|Chill|Chill+}} gives ''at least'' one extra Orb always in your starting hand.\n\n* {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, and {{P|Potion of Capacity}} give additional Orb Slots, giving Fission a much higher potential output.\n\n* The large amount of {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' generated by Fission can be used to play other expensive and X cost cards, such as {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Reinforced Body}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}}.\n\n* As Fission+ {{KW|Evoke|Evokes}} all of your Orbs, {{BD|Focus}} can substantially improve its output: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Reducing the amount of Orb Slots through {{C|Consume}} reduces the potential of {{C|Fission}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Fission+ evoking Orbs in reverse order.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 41: Chill'''\n** Fission now costs 0.\n** Fission+ now Evokes all orbs rather than removing.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\nFission card reworked.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2291":{"pageid":2291,"ns":0,"title":"Follow-Up","revisions":[{"revid":55432,"parentid":53385,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Follow-Up\n|Image       = Purple-Follow-Up.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;11) damage. <br>If the previous card played was an Attack, gain {{Icon|PE}}.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{C|Follow-Up}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (11 if upgraded) damage. If the last card played this combat was an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}, this card also gives 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* No matter what {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{C|Follow-Up}} has, the player will always gain 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if it is played when the last card played this combat was an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}. This can be used to your advantage by reducing the cost below 1, but can lose you {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' as well if the cost is increased. The cost can be changed by:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Setup}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' gain, although this extra energy is often useless.\n* {{C|Madness}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* If {{C|Follow-Up}} is selected from an {{P|Attack Potion}} it will have a cost of 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{R|Snecko Eye}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}} will randomize the cost from 0 to 3, which can result in a neutral, gained or lost amount of energy.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2133":{"pageid":2133,"ns":0,"title":"Force Field","revisions":[{"revid":53381,"parentid":50589,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Force Field\n|Image       = Blue-ForceField.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 4\n|Description = Costs 1 less {{Icon|BE}} for each Power card played this combat.<br>Gain (12;16) {{KW|Block}}.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Force Field}} is a 4 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 12 (16 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}. This card costs 1 less {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' for every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card that was played previously this combat. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card, most notably {{C|Echo Form}}, as it allows other {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} to be played twice.\n* Using {{C|Amplify}} to play {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards twice also lowers the cost of this card twice.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2071":{"pageid":2071,"ns":0,"title":"Go for the Eyes","revisions":[{"revid":55803,"parentid":50561,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Go for the Eyes\n|Image       = Blue-GofortheEyes.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (3;4) damage.<br>If the enemy intends to attack, apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{C|Go for the Eyes}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 3 (4 if upgraded) damage. If the target's [[Intent]] is to attack, apply 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* When the enemy's [[Intent]] is obscured by {{R|Runic Dome}}, it can be harder to know if this card will have an effect if there are multiple enemies. {{C|Go for the Eyes}} will be highlighted if at least one enemy's [[Intent]] is to attack, but there is no way of knowing which enemy before playing it. However, {{C|Go for the Eyes}} can still be played on any target, and this can be used to determine if the target is attacking when you are unsure.\n\n* It does not matter if the target's attack has an additional effect or deals 0 damage, as long as attacking is part of the [[Intent]], this card will activate its effects.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{C|Go for the Eyes}} is the only [[Defect]] card that applies {{BD|Weak}}, making it the class with the lowest number of cards applying {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1875":{"pageid":1875,"ns":0,"title":"Lesson Learned","revisions":[{"revid":56414,"parentid":56118,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Lesson Learned\n| Image       = Purple-LessonLearned.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (10;13) damage. <br>If {{KW|Fatal}}, {{KW|Upgrade}} a random card in your deck. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| Keywords    = Deck\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Upgrade\n| InteractsWith = Fatal\n}}\n{{C|Lesson Learned}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 10 (13 if upgraded) damage, and if this damage is {{KW|Fatal}}, it will permanently {{KW|Upgrade}} a random card in your deck. {{C|Lesson Learned}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As playing {{C|Lesson Learned}} at the right moment is crucial, it synergizes with {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and ways to {{KW|Retain}} it, such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, {{C|Equilibrium}} or {{C|Meditate}}.\n\n* As one of the few cards that has benefits that remain outside of combat, triggering it as often as possible becomes an additional objective within combat. Given that {{C|Lesson Learned}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after use, it synergizes with:\n** {{R|Strange Spoon}}, which gives a 50% chance to not {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Lesson Learned}} when played, allowing it to be redrawn and used again.\n** {{C|Exhume}}, which can get {{C|Lesson Learned}} back once after being played, with the added benefit of putting it directly into your hand.\n\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}} can mitigate the downside of {{R|Fusion Hammer}}, as it often fully upgrades your deck over time.\n\n* As you have less need to use [[Map Locations#Rest_Sites|Rest Sites]] for upgrading, {{R|Girya}}, {{R|Peace Pipe}} and {{R|Shovel}}, the relics that give alternate actions at [[Rest Site|Rest Sites]], become better.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* When duplicated through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Lesson Learned}} will trigger its {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.\n** As duplicated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} always target the same enemy with both plays, you cannot trigger {{C|Lesson Learned}} twice by duplicating it.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} does ''not'' trigger when {{BD|Minion|Minions}} are killed.\n** However, the {{M|Cultist}} enemies in {{M|Awakened One}} fight are not technically {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, and ''can'' trigger {{KW|Fatal}}.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} is not affected by {{M|Slime Boss}} or other Slime enemies splitting, and only triggers when reducing a Slime's health to 0, whether that Slime was spawned as the result of a split or not.\n* The first phase of {{M|Awakened One}} does not trigger {{KW|Fatal}}, but the second phase does.\n\n* In the {{M|Darkling|Three Darklings}} fight, an attack is only considered {{KW|Fatal}} if it kills the last {{M|Darkling}}; otherwise, unlimited triggers could be farmed on this fight.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} triggers on killing the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}, although this does not matter, as it ends the run.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Lesson Learned}} tends to lead to your deck being fully upgraded late game, it reduces the effectiveness of {{C|Apotheosis}}, {{C|Armaments}} and {{R|Warped Tongs}}.\n\n* Due to the limited number of {{KW|Fatal}} triggers available in any given combat, {{C|Lesson Learned}} does not synergize with other {{KW|Fatal}} cards:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Hand of Greed}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n* {{C|Feed}}\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2462":{"pageid":2462,"ns":0,"title":"Magnetism","revisions":[{"revid":55849,"parentid":55454,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Magnetism|Spectrum Shift}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Magnetism\n|Image       = Colorless-Magnetism.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|CostPlus    = 1\n|Description = At the start of your turn, add a random Colorless card into your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Magnetism}}{{C|Magnetism}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Magnetism}}, which adds a random {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card at the start of every turn.\n\n== Obtaining Magnetism ==\n{{C|Magnetism}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Magnetism}} takes effect before your cards are drawn. This means that having a high amount of {{BD|Magnetism}} can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}\n* {{C|Apparition}}\n* {{C|Bite}}\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}} \n* {{C|Shiv}}\n* {{C|Beta}}\n* {{C|Insight}}\n* {{C|Miracle}}\n* {{C|Omega}}\n* {{C|Safety}}\n* {{C|Smite}}\n* {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Capitalization fixes for Magnetism power description.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Magnetism power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** New colorless card: Magnetism.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1855":{"pageid":1855,"ns":0,"title":"Master Reality","revisions":[{"revid":56401,"parentid":55852,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Master Reality\n| Image       = Purple-MasterReality.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Whenever a card is created during combat, {{KW|Upgrade}} it.\n| GivesToPlayer = Upgrade\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Master Reality}}{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}\n{{C|Master Reality}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives one {{BD|Master Reality}}, which {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} any card created during combat. As {{BD|Master Reality}} does not stack, copies of {{C|Master Reality}} played after the first have no additional effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with anything that creates cards that can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} during combat:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Evaluate}}, {{C|Carve Reality}}, {{C|Deceive Reality}}, {{C|Foreign Influence}}, {{C|Pray}}, {{C|Reach Heaven}},  {{C|Conjure Blade}}, {{C|Deus Ex Machina}}.\n* {{C|Battle Hymn}} and {{C|Study}} will generate a card every turn.\n* {{C|Alpha}}, which will generate {{C|Beta}}, which will in turn generate {{C|Omega}}.\n* {{C|Discovery}}, {{C|Jack of All Trades}}, {{C|Chrysalis}}, {{C|Magnetism}}, {{C|Metamorphosis}}, {{C|Transmutation}}.\n\n* {{C|Anger}}, {{C|Dual Wield}} and {{C|Infernal Blade}}. \n* {{C|Blade Dance}}, {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}, {{C|Distraction}}, {{C|Endless Agony}}, {{C|Infinite Blades}}, {{C|Nightmare}}, {{C|Storm of Steel}}.\n* {{C|Hello World}}, {{C|White Noise}}, {{C|Creative AI}}.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Dead Branch}}\n* {{R|Nilry's Codex}}\n\n==== c) Potions ====\n* {{P|Attack Potion}}\n* {{P|Colorless Potion}}\n* {{P|Power Potion}}\n* {{P|Skill Potion}}\n* {{P|Bottled Miracle}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Only cards created after playing {{C|Master Reality}} will be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}}.\n\n* Although {{C|Burn}} has an upgraded version, it cannot be upgraded by the player, and is therefore unaffected by {{C|Master Reality}}.\n\n* The {{BD|Master Reality}} buff does not stack, meaning {{C|Searing Blow}} can usually only be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} once.\n\n* While {{C|Master Reality}} is active, {{C|Exhume}} will '''not''' upgrade the card it brings back.\n\n== Bugs ==\n* Under the effect of {{C|Master Reality}}, {{C|Dual Wield}} {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} '''all''' cards, even the original card that was copied.\n\n* If {{C|Searing Blow}} is generated with {{BD|Master Reality}} active, it will generate with +2 {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} instead of +1, unless generated by {{C|Foreign Influence}} or {{R|Nilry's Codex}}. \n** This can be replicated without {{R|Prismatic Shard}} or {{E|A Note For Yourself}}, by generating {{C|Searing Blow}} with {{C|Foreign Influence}} as [[The Watcher]] in the [[Bronze Automaton]] combat. Allowing one of its minions to steal {{C|Searing Blow}} and then retrieving it by killing that minion counts as that {{C|Searing Blow}} being generated.\n*** This can be used to achieve a maximum of +5 {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}}: +1 through initial generation via {{C|Foreign Influence}}, and +2 through both minions.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1923":{"pageid":1923,"ns":0,"title":"Metallicize","revisions":[{"revid":56747,"parentid":55859,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Metallicize\n| Image       = Red-Metallicize.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = At the end of your turn, gain (3;4) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Metallicize\n| PowerGives = Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Metallicize\n| Image        = Icon Metallicize.png\n| Description  = At the end of every turn, gain X {{KW|Block}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Metallicize}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Metallicize}}, which grants that amount of {{KW|Block}} at the end of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Metallicize}} gives {{KW|Block}} ''after'' {{R|Orichalcum}} checks if you have block, meaning {{BD|Metallicize}} does not prevent the relic from activating.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Metallicize}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42'''\n** Updating SFX for Metallicize Power.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1453":{"pageid":1453,"ns":0,"title":"Neutralize","revisions":[{"revid":56334,"parentid":55869,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Neutralize\n| Image       = Green-Neutralize.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Deal (3;4) damage.<br>Apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Weak\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{C|Neutralize}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 3 (4 if upgraded) damage and applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Obtaining Neutralize ==\nThe [[Silent]] starts the game with one copy of {{C|Neutralize}} in her deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards, but can be obtained in the {{E|Match and Keep}} Event. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Krane}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Weak}}.\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of this card by 4.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Cloak and Dagger no longer appears in the card match event before it is unlocked, instead there is always a copy of Neutralize.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2032":{"pageid":2032,"ns":0,"title":"Predator","revisions":[{"revid":55905,"parentid":50518,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Predator\n|Image       = Green-Predator.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (15;20) damage.<br>Next turn, draw 2 additional cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Draw Card}}{{C|Predator}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Three {{M|Sentry|Sentries}} are prominently featured in the card art.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2205":{"pageid":2205,"ns":0,"title":"Sunder","revisions":[{"revid":55503,"parentid":53383,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sunder\n|Image       = Blue-Sunder.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = Deal (24;32) damage.<br>If this kills an enemy, gain {{Icon|BE}} {{Icon|BE}} {{Icon|BE}}.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{C|Sunder}} is a 3 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 24 (32 if upgraded) damage. If it kills an enemy, minion or not, you gain 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* No matter what {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{C|Sunder}} has, the player will always gain 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' if it kills an enemy. This can be used to your advantage by reducing the cost below 3. The cost can be changed by:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Setup}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' gain, although this extra energy is often useless.\n* {{C|Enlightenment}} sets the cost to 1, resulting in 2 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Madness}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* If {{C|Sunder}} is selected from an {{P|Attack Potion}} it will have a cost of 0, resulting in 3 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{R|Snecko Eye}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}} will randomize the cost from 0 to 3, which can result in a neutral or gained amount of energy.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed double-played Sunder gaining energy twice on Darklings and Awakened One.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}